{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ושמעו", :translit "v'shim'u", :gloss "and hear"} {:he "שמע", :translit "shema", :gloss "hear"} {:he "שמע ישראל", :translit "shema yisra'el", :gloss "Hear O Israel"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The word ושמעו is read as שמע plus an extra ו; the verse thus alludes to שמע ישראל, which the Ba'al HaTurim counts as six words (including the ו of ושמעו as alluding to six)."}], :frame {:text "The Shema prayer is built from Deuteronomy 6:4–9, and the first verse שמע ישראל ה׳ אלהינו ה׳ אחד contains six words. The tradition that Jacob our patriarch assembled his sons and recited the Shema — or that his name Yisra'el encodes that declaration — appears in midrashic sources discussing Genesis 49:2.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 6:4" "Bereshit Rabbah 98:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ושמעו בני יעקב", :translit "v'shim'u b'nei ya'akov", :gloss "and hear, sons of Jacob"} {:he "ושמעו", :translit "v'shim'u", :gloss "and hear"} {:he "ביקש לגלות הקץ", :translit "bikesh legalot ha-ketz", :gloss "he sought to reveal the End"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ושמעו", :b "ביקש לגלות הקץ"}], :frame {:text "The motif that Jacob wished to reveal the time of the ultimate redemption (the keitz) to his sons but the divine presence departed from him is recorded in the Talmud's exposition of Genesis 49:1, where the verse introduces Jacob's final words to his children.", :sources ["Pesachim 56a" "Genesis 49:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ושמעו אל ישראל", :translit "v'shim'u el yisra'el", :gloss "and hear, unto Israel"} {:he "קצו של מלך המשיח", :translit "kitzo shel melekh ha-mashiach", :gloss "the end of King Messiah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ושמעו אל ישראל", :b "קצו של מלך המשיח"}], :frame {:text "Daniel 7:13–14 describes one like a son of man receiving everlasting dominion, and Daniel 9:25–26 speaks of an 'anointed one' (mashiach) linked to a decreed end-time. Rabbinic readings connect these passages to the figure of King Messiah and his appointed era.", :sources ["Daniel 7:13–14" "Daniel 9:25–26"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The word ושמעו is read as שמע plus an extra ו; the verse thus alludes to שמע ישראל, which the Ba'al HaTurim counts as six words (including the ו of ושמעו as alluding to six).", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ושמעו", :a-value 422, :b "ביקש לגלות הקץ", :b-value 1076, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ושמעו אל ישראל", :a-value 994, :b "קצו של מלך המשיח", :b-value 979, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:12:15.571387027Z", :model "glm-5.2"}